# Copy to .env for local development. Never commit the real .env.
#
# EXPO_PUBLIC_* vars are inlined into the JS bundle at build time, so
# this is visible to anyone who inspects the app — never put a secret
# here. It's exactly why the API URL (public by nature) is the only
# thing the app needs to know about its backend.
#
# - Physical device on the same Wi-Fi as your machine: use your LAN IP,
#   e.g. http://192.168.1.23:4000/graphql (find it with `ipconfig`).
# - Android emulator: http://10.0.2.2:4000/graphql
# - Production (Netlify web build / EAS preview build): the Render URL.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:4000/graphql
